    <string name="dialog_lyrics_title">Lyrics</string>
    <string name="dialog_lyrics_message">With Lyrics on, the title and artist of the song that is playing are sent to lrclib.net to find its lyrics. Nothing else leaves this TV.\n\nWhile a song plays, press Down on the remote to see the lyrics, and Up or Back to close them.</string>
    <string name="dialog_sleep_title">Sleep after music</string>
    <string name="dialog_sleep_message">When AirPlay turns this TV on and nobody uses the remote, the TV can go back to sleep a few minutes after the music ends.\n\nAndroid allows this only through an accessibility service, which has to be switched on once from a computer:\n\nadb shell settings put secure enabled_accessibility_services %1$s\nadb shell settings put secure accessibility_enabled 1\n\nIf other accessibility services are on already, add this one to the colon-separated list instead. The service does not read the screen.</string>
    <string name="sleep_service_label" translatable="false">AirPlay TV sleep</string>
    <string name="sleep_service_description">Lets AirPlay TV put the TV back to sleep after the music. It does not read the screen or see what you do.</string>
    <string name="setting_remote_volume">Remote Volume Keys</string>
    <string name="value_tv">TV</string>
    <string name="value_airplay">AirPlay</string>
    <string name="dialog_remote_volume_title">Remote volume keys</string>
    <string name="dialog_remote_volume_message">For streaming sticks whose volume buttons do not change the sound: while something plays over AirPlay, the remote’s volume and mute buttons change the AirPlay volume instead.\n\nLeave this on TV if the buttons already work.</string>

